WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.525
Each of these dangers
has a guard in the code.

2
00:00:02.525 --> 00:00:05.068
The headline one is
still the wrong subject,

3
00:00:05.068 --> 00:00:09.025
caught by the claims check and the
exchange test before any cutover.

4
00:00:09.025 --> 00:00:12.513
Others are small: a trailing
slash, a stray space,

5
00:00:12.513 --> 00:00:15.375
a subject guessed instead of captured.

6
00:00:15.375 --> 00:00:19.288
Some are about timing, like
creating credentials in parallel,

7
00:00:19.288 --> 00:00:21.513
or using one before it's propagated.

8
00:00:21.513 --> 00:00:25.399
And some are about keeping your
way back: the code never deletes,

9
00:00:25.399 --> 00:00:29.062
so the rollback, re-enabling
the old account, always remains.

10
00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:32.660
Notice that writes stay with a
person, never a standing app.
